📘 Kubernetes Bare-Metal Setup Guide
(Ingress-NGINX + MetalLB LoadBalancer)
1️⃣ Prerequisites

Kubernetes cluster (single or multi-node)     

kubectl configured

Nodes in private network (example: 192.168.122.0/24)

Internet access for pulling images

2️⃣ Install Ingress Controller (NGINX)

Install Ingress controller in bare-metal mode.

kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/main/deploy/static/provider/baremetal/deploy.yaml
Check services
kubectl get svc -n ingress-nginx

You will see:

ingress-nginx-controller   NodePort

Example:

80:32143/TCP, 443:32325/TCP
3️⃣ Test Ingress using NodePort (initial access)

If no LoadBalancer exists yet:

http://<node-ip>:<node-port>

Example:

http://192.168.122.131:32143
4️⃣ Install MetalLB (Bare-Metal LoadBalancer)

MetalLB provides LoadBalancer IPs for on-prem clusters.

Install MetalLB
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/metallb/metallb/main/config/manifests/metallb-native.yaml
Verify pods
kubectl get pods -n metallb-system

Expected:

controller Running
speaker Running
5️⃣ Configure MetalLB IP Pool

Create config file:

apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: default-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
  - 192.168.122.200-192.168.122.220
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: L2Advertisement
metadata:
  name: default-advertisement
  namespace: metallb-system

Apply:

kubectl apply -f metallb-config.yaml
6️⃣ Patch Ingress Service to LoadBalancer
kubectl patch svc ingress-nginx-controller -n ingress-nginx \
  -p '{"spec": {"type": "LoadBalancer"}}'
Verify External IP
kubectl get svc -n ingress-nginx

Expected:

EXTERNAL-IP: 192.168.122.200
7️⃣ Create Ingress Rule

Example ingress:

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: nginx-ingress
spec:
  rules:
  - host: nginx.local
    http:
      paths:
      - path: /
        pathType: Prefix
        backend:
          service:
            name: nginx
            port:
              number: 80

Apply:

kubectl apply -f nginx-ingress.yaml
8️⃣ DNS Setup (Local Testing)

Add entry in your local machine:

sudo nano /etc/hosts

Add:

192.168.122.200 nginx.local
9️⃣ Final Access Test

Try in browser:

http://nginx.local

OR:

http://nginx.local:80
